course: dictionary
lesson: 8638
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word sea can mean a huge area of salt water, a named part of that water, or a large amount of something. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The ship sailed out to sea.» Here sea means the salt water that covers most of the Earth.
explain: «We sailed across the North Sea.» The words North Sea name one particular area of salt water, so the meaning is the second one. Now try the third meaning: «A sea of faces turned to look at me.» Faces are not water, so sea must mean a large amount, a huge crowd.
explain: Some phrases use sea in a special way. «Ella was all at sea with the new maths sums.» Ella was not on a boat. All at sea means confused. Always check: does my meaning still make sense in this sentence?
fact: Sea means a large area of salt water that covers most of the Earth.
fact: A particular sea has a name, such as «the North Sea» or «the Mediterranean Sea».
fact: Sea can also mean a large amount of something, as in «a sea of faces».
fact: «All at sea» means confused, and «out to sea» means away from the land, over the water.
fact: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster, so railings by the sea rust quickly.» Always swim between the flags, and never swim alone.
exercise: «The sea was calm and blue all morning.» What does sea mean here? | A kind of boat | A large amount of something | *The large area of salt water that covers most of the Earth | A small pond in a garden
exercise: «Sicily is the biggest island in the Mediterranean Sea.» What kind of sea is the Mediterranean? | *A particular large area of salt water | A sea of faces | A large amount of something | A fish that swims in rivers
exercise: «A sea of faces turned to look at her.» What does sea mean in this sentence? | *A large crowd, a huge amount of faces | A wave that crashes on the beach | The salt water that covers most of the Earth | A cold, wet wind
test: «Ben was all at sea when the teacher changed the test date.» What does all at sea mean? | Very hot and sunny | Ready to leave for the beach | *Confused | Swimming in the sea
test: What does seashell mean? | A shiny stone from a river | A sea of shells on a shop shelf | *A shell that comes from the sea | A shell for a boat
exam: Read this: «The sea rose and fell all day, and the hall was a sea of faces.» How many different meanings of sea are used in this text? | One | *Two | None | Three
